        "id": "one-anomaly-is-enough",
        "statement": "One odd run is enough to name the fault.",
        "remediation": "Drag on the track also slows the cart at 2 N. The 3 N run is what tells them apart."
      },
      {
        "id": "unfair-comparison-isolates-a-cause",
        "statement": "A run where two things changed still pins down one cause.",
        "remediation": "Each pair of runs moved only the force dial, so only the force is under test."
      },
      {
        "id": "sibling-compared-under-different-conditions",
        "statement": "The odd cart is faulty because it is slower than a cart tested another way.",
        "remediation": "Both carts were run at 2 N and at 3 N, so the dial was not the difference."
      }
    ],
    "debriefExplanation": "The odd cart sped up by the same amount at 2 N and at 3 N. A cart with extra cargo would have sped up more at the higher force. A cart with a stuck thruster keeps the same small push no matter what the dial says, so the result never changes. A flat pair of speed lines is the tell.",
